,1)) for solids (186-221); placement \"pattern\" solid → drawSolidPattern full-panel fills (279-289); dispatch at 318-334; cutouts destination-out after all paint (335-339).\n\n**src/project/archive.ts (298 lines)**: saveProject validates isValidProjectDocument then JSON.stringify(document) (layers incl. transform serialized verbatim); openProject accepts schemaVersion 1 (migrate) or 2; old pattern-solid docs round-trip.\n\n**docs/2026-08-30-direct-rectangle-editing-design.md (117 lines)**: NORMATIVE line 33: \"Dragging a side handle moves only that edge along the rectangle's local axis while the opposite edge stays fixed. This changes one dimension and shifts the center by half the dragged distance. Same rule after rotation.\" Also: 4 side handles + corner + rotate handle; 44px hit targets; handle hit priority over interior drag; min size prevents edge crossing; More sheet drops Wide/Tall for color rects and cutouts, two-column layout; old full-clothing solids unchanged/non-transformable/no recreation; color rect may extend beyond canvas (render clipped); one undo entry per drag; cancel restores geometry.\n\n## KEY FINDING (verified by algebra + test numbers) — BLOCKER candidate\nThe edge-resize implementation has 2× gain, violating the design's \"center shifts by half the dragged distance\". With pointer local coordinate p (relative to gesture-start center) and startHalf s: correct math (opposite edge fixed AND dragged edge under pointer) requires newWidth = p + s, newHalf = (p+s)/2, center shift = (p−s)/2. Implemented: half = max(minHalf, p), scaleX = 2p, shift = p − s. Consequence: opposite edge stays fixed ✓, but center shifts by the FULL drag distance and the dragged edge overshoots the pointer by exactly the drag distance (edge moves 2× pointer speed — broken direct manipulation on touch). Evidence from tests (which encode the buggy math, hence green): dragging right handle of a 400px-wide rect (center 256, half 200) from x=456 to x=506 (+50px) expects scaleX=500, positionX=306 (tests/browser/gestures.test.ts \"side handle drags resize one edge...\" drags array, ~line 939-963); correct values would be scaleX=450, positionX=281 (edges: 281−225=56 fixed, 281+225=506 under pointer). Rotated cutout test (90°, drag (256,456)→(256,496), expects width 480/centerY 296; correct: width 440/centerY 278). Clamp test expects scaleX≈0.01/positionX≈56.005. Same 2× gain applies to cutouts via cutoutPatchFromTransformPatch mapping (mapping itself is consistent). Fix: scaleX = clamp(startHalfWidth + p, MIN_ITEM_SCALE, ∞) [i.e., p ≥ MIN_ITEM_SCALE − startHalfWidth], shift = (p − startHalfWidth)/2 (analogous Y axis), then rotate shift back — and update the test expectations.\n\n## Verified-OK so far (no findings)\nHit order rotate→corner→edge→move correct; raster excluded from edge loop (tested \"edge midpoint drags on a raster sticker move it\"); handleRadiusCanvasPx conversion correct; wheel+keyboard gated by directlyEditable (decal solids in, pattern solids out); duplicate/undo/redo/cap all sound; no resurrection path for full-clothing solids; More sheet field visibility matches settled decisions per kind; Size ratio commit round-trips; nonce resync resets invalid input; compositor + archive compat intact; edge handles not bounds-clamped like scale/rotate handles but corners aren't either and pointer capture keeps them grabbable (cosmetic at most); \"Color\" label reuses cutout-selection-label class (cosmetic)."}]}
